  "notes": "Surface derived 2026-07-26 from the Pointer Events Editor's Draft (merged via w3c/pointerevents PR #643): one attribute (WheelEvent.momentum) and one dictionary field (WheelEventInit.momentum). After independent review: the two contracts are kept distinct \u2014 per-event platform value (Chromium maps momentum_phase != kPhaseNone; unit test injects Began/Changed/None; the implementing CL 7869775 records Linux manual testing did not surface the value, so hardware/OS coverage needs real 151+ evidence) versus constructor/WebIDL behavior (boolean default false; ToBoolean conversion makes the string 'false' truthy; omitted defaults; unknown members ignored; authored events echo the value, with isTrusted as the authored-vs-native distinction). Privacy review is Pending; fingerprinting claims are framed as unreviewed. Both dead spec anchors documented (ChromeStatus #dom-wheelevent-momentum; BCD #dom-wheeleventinit-momentum). Deliberately partial pending independent review."
